= The 60-Second Self-Test

Cover the answers, say each one aloud, then check. If any answer takes longer than ten seconds, revisit that section.

- *Six sources of human capital — name them.* → Education, health, on-the-job training, study programmes, migration, information.
- *Cooperative society vs moneylender — which is institutional?* → Cooperative; moneylenders are non-institutional.
- *Why do farmers sell right after harvest?* → No storage — distress sales at low prices; warehousing is the fix.
- *Largest worker category in India?* → Self-employed — ahead of casual and regular salaried.
- *MGNREGA guarantees what, to whom?* → 100 days of wage work per rural household per year (2005).
- *The environment's "sink" function means…?* → Absorbing and digesting waste — until capacity overflows.

